    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed roster availability, forcing us to lean heavily on **Junior Caminero**, who anchors the lineup with a 74.83 score. Facing Shawn Armstrong, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a soft 4.35 xERA matchup and a projected #3 slot in the order. While his lineup position is technically pending, the confluence of high-leverage recency data and the platoon advantage against the right-handed Armstrong keeps his floor high. He remains our primary engine for R and RBI production in a day where the rest of the core, including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, are sidelined due to the team\u2019s off-day schedule.\n\nIn assessing the depth chart for future rotation, **Caleb Durbin** and **Kazuma Okamoto** continue to press for inclusion based on their elite sprint speed profiles, though today\u2019s roster construction limits their impact. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** and **Colt Keith** remain on the periphery of the starting cut, narrowly missing out due to the scarcity of high-efficiency matchup windows. **Lars Nootbaar** and **Hector Rodriguez** possess the necessary contact profiles to move into the 60+ tier if the lineup congestion clears, but for now, they are relegated to the bench to preserve our seasonal game caps. We are monitoring **Gary Sanchez** and **Josh Smith** closely; should the game-day park factors shift\u2014specifically regarding wind velocity\u2014we may look to optimize **Dillon Dingler** or **Carson Benge** for their defensive versatility and late-game substitution potential.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of our secondary prospects like **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**. While **Christian Yelich** offers elite category weight when active, our current focus is strictly on maximizing the efficiency of **Junior Caminero** while holding steady on our bench depth. We will avoid ove